h films have a  religious historical setting and both  involve a member of the church arriving  at a strange place to solve a mysterious  murder one major difference in the nun a  supernatural force is actually behind  the mayhem get to know Valli the nun is  a product of James wons imagination but  the demonic being is rooted in real-life  lore the demons name gives us power rich  in the classic occult texts the Lesser  Key of Solomon Ballack has given the  title grande president of hell and  assumes the form of a winged child  riding a two-headed dragon that sounds  epic but maybe not for a haunted house  movie  so far VALIC has taken multiple forms in  the conjuring universe in fact the demon  briefly becomes the crooked man in the  conjuring 2  does this mean Edie and Lorraine Warren  will eventually have a final showdown  with a creepy kid on a dragon let's hope  not Vande equals buzz in the early days  of YouTube jump scare videos were all  over the place like a throwback to those  simpler times a controversial  seven-second ad appeared on YouTube a  few weeks before the nones release date  first a volume icon appeared in the  middle of the users screen viewers were  only given a few seconds before a  shrieking nun popped up to scare the  bejesus out of them the ad didn't sit  well with everyone one Twitter user even  suggested it could be dangerous writing  if you see an ad on YouTube with the  volume sign being turned down and  nothing else it's a jump scare for the  new nun movie coming out please retweet  to save a life the warning was retweeted  over 100,000 times forcing YouTube to  respond the company removed the ad for  violating its shocking content policy  which was ultimately fantastic publicity  for the film  thanks jump-scare truth or scare during  her comic-con interview with  Entertainment Tonight taissa farmiga  explained why she's frightened by the  occult I don't know what I believe about  supernatural and ghosts but on the kind  of person that's like why open the doors  when I let it in because then I'll get  an answer and I don't want a definite  answer the one person who really seems  to believe in ghosts is Koren Hardy in  fact he told cinema blend he saw two  real ghosts while filming a scene in a  Romanian fortress I go into the room and  as I went into the room I see these two  guys from the crew you know I'm probably  sound Department just so sitting a  little further back in the dark  arty says he greeted the men and then  sat with his back to them while getting  a shot but the real terror was yet to  come  half an hour later he turned around and  there was just no one in the room and  then and there haven't been anyone in  there after look there's no way they  could have come we can only guess what  happened next  you  [Music]
 

